      "content": "Walnut, being a dense and sometimes tricky wood, can be quite stubborn, especially in the tight confines of dovetail pins. Beyond moisture and angle, irregular splintering can sometimes be a sign of hidden stresses or minor inconsistencies in the wood itself. Look closely for any areas where the grain direction abruptly changes, or where there might be a tiny, almost invisible inclusion or knot—even a minuscule one can act like a weak point. It's a bit like trying to carve a path through a swarm of tiny, unpredictable little things.",
